"""
Panel FGLS (xtgls), panel-corrected standard errors (xtpcse), AR(1) fixed/random effects (xtregar) and the
Hausman–Taylor / Amemiya–MaCurdy estimator (xthtaylor) — tests/test_panel_fgls.py

Primary reference: Stata 19.5 (StataNow MP, batch mode), do-files and logs kept outside the repository
(xtgls.do, xtpcse.do, xtregar.do, xthtaylor.do; values dumped with %24.17g by dump.do).  Data were read with
`import delimited ..., asdouble`, firms encoded alphabetically (encode firm) and `xtset fid year` / `xtset id year`.

Data
    sample_data/Grunfeld_Panel.csv (11 firms x 20 years) and three variants built by the rules in the fixtures:
        unbal   drop if mod(year*7 + (fid-1)*3, 11) == 0      (internal gaps in every firm; tests/test_panel_extended.py)
        unbal2  drop firm 1 <= 1936, firm 3 in 1954, firm 5 in 1945   (periods common to all firms exist)
        short   keep if year <= 1942                           (T = 8 < m = 11: singular Σ̂ for panels(correlated))
        single  unbal with invest missing for firm 2 after 1935 (a panel with one observation)
    sample_data/Panel_HT_Wage.csv (300 workers x 7 years, generator sample_data/make_panel_ht_sample_data.py) and
        unbal   drop if mod(id*3 + year, 7) == 0 & id <= 150

Commands
    xtgls invest value capital, panels(iid|hetero|corr) [corr(ar1|psar1) rhotype(dw|freg|tscorr|theil|nagar) igls
          iterate() tolerance() nmk force noconstant]
    xtpcse invest value capital, [correlation(independent|ar1|psar1) rhotype(dw|freg|tscorr) np1 hetonly
          independent pairwise nmk noconstant]
    xtregar invest value capital, fe|re [lbi rhotype(regress|freg|tscorr|theil|nagar|onestep) twostep rhof(0.5)]
    xthtaylor lwage wks south occ exper union female rural educ, endog(exper union educ) [amacurdy small
          constant(female rural educ) vce(robust) noconstant];  xtreg ..., fe + hausman fe ht
Secondary reference: the printed examples of [XT] xtpcse and [XT] xtregar (Stata's grunfeld = this file without
American Steel).
Values are hard-coded below (Stata is not needed to run the tests).
"""
